                        ],
                        "form": "paniekjes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d6927ac-c262-3f3f-bc21-88c323465f44",
                        "entry_id": "35229c3d-ca13-305c-b7b8-ccb59d16bc7f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "plotselinge hevige schrik voor een echt of vermeend gevaar"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "44d4e9e3-5f79-48f6-8d39-9fe89799493f",
                                "sense_id": "9d6927ac-c262-3f3f-bc21-88c323465f44",
                                "text": "Hij zucht en steunt en dan brult hij. Paniek maakt zich van hem meester. Hij voelt tranen opwellen, slaat met zijn vuist tegen de muur van leem."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cd817b9-3eb4-4f87-99ba-4a1030cd1d63",
                                "sense_id": "9d6927ac-c262-3f3f-bc21-88c323465f44",
                                "text": "De tropische storm Bonnie die Aruba, Bonaire en Curaçao mogelijk zal treffen, komt waarschijnlijk niet woensdagavond maar al in de middag (plaatselijke tijd) aan land op de eilanden. Dat zegt het Caribbean Weather Center (CWC) woensdag tegen NU.nl. Daardoor is op het eiland paniek ontstaan onder de inwoners."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d4b1bc4f-455e-454e-876a-7cad3ae9d278",
                        "source_entry_id": "35229c3d-ca13-305c-b7b8-ccb59d16bc7f",
                        "source_sense_id": "9d6927ac-c262-3f3f-bc21-88c323465f44",
                        "target_lang_word": "panic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "panic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "237933f2-ce86-3746-bf6c-f44f49998cf7",
                                        "entry_id": "fb376fad-bd33-3500-8c1d-5a7ed18a9540",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of Panic (“pertaining to the Greek god Pan”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "42fee9f1-ebf8-36f1-95ec-9b85f352a134",
                                        "entry_id": "fb376fad-bd33-3500-8c1d-5a7ed18a9540",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of fear, fright, etc: overwhelming or sudden."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a005997e-7031-4c7b-9267-79b3f3ce4c36",
                                                "sense_id": "42fee9f1-ebf8-36f1-95ec-9b85f352a134",
                                                "text": "All things were there in a diſordered confuſion, and in a confuſed furie, vntill ſuch time as by prayers and ſacrifices they had appeaſed the wrath of their Gods. They call it to this day, the P[a]nike terror."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3747e620-fe3a-4db7-b65c-1f0d01fa4689",
                                                "sense_id": "42fee9f1-ebf8-36f1-95ec-9b85f352a134",
                                                "text": "So long as Epaminondas was captaine general of the Thebans, there was never ſeene in his campe any of theſe ſudden fooliſh frights, without any certeine cauſe, which they call Panique Terrores."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "641769ac-6109-4790-8f5a-a88b2347fdf3",
                                                "sense_id": "42fee9f1-ebf8-36f1-95ec-9b85f352a134",
                                                "text": "But why dwell I ſo intolerable long about Tolerations, I hope my feares are but panick, againſt which I have a double cordiall."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eeea3e0a-2420-4187-8a19-2046546387f7",
                                                "sense_id": "42fee9f1-ebf8-36f1-95ec-9b85f352a134",
                                                "text": "[L]ike a couragious Captain does all he can to imbody his Army; he perſwades, threats, oppoſes, and cries aloud, that albeit Bickermanſe was ſlain yet He was living; yea that many as good Officers as Bickermanſe were in the Army; But in vain; for ſuch was their diſorder and pannick fear, that impoſſible it was to revoke them: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9e05dd7-0c74-4542-85fb-e732cfee63d6",
                                                "sense_id": "42fee9f1-ebf8-36f1-95ec-9b85f352a134",
                                                "text": "Suſpicion, with Sedition join'd, are near;\n And Rumors rais'd, and Murmurs mix'd, and Panique Fear."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d10c6b9-5ea5-4864-9928-a882594f08a4",
                                                "sense_id": "42fee9f1-ebf8-36f1-95ec-9b85f352a134",
                                                "text": "At that moment a flight of birds passed close overhead, and at the whirr of their wings a panic fear seized her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "606e1305-a1b9-4b22-b64e-d0926f4c734c",
                                                "sense_id": "42fee9f1-ebf8-36f1-95ec-9b85f352a134",
                                                "text": "Terrified, he looked down from the skies\n At the waves, and panic blackness filled his eyes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e7f29d8-0251-3ca7-b6aa-4d45a614c7e4",
                                        "entry_id": "fb376fad-bd33-3500-8c1d-5a7ed18a9540",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to or resulting from overwhelming fear or fright."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3f3d3d9-9dfe-457b-9e04-cb5bd1f1c11d",
                                                "sense_id": "5e7f29d8-0251-3ca7-b6aa-4d45a614c7e4",
                                                "text": "[H]e perceived how that many women followed his ſouldiers, ſome being their wives, and ſome wanting nothing to make them ſo but marriage, […] The King coming to a great river, after his men and the wagons were paſſed over, cauſed the bridge to be broken down, hoping ſo to be rid of theſe feminine impediments; but they on a ſudden liſt up a panick ſhrick which pierced the skies, and the ſouldiers hearts on the other ſide of the river, who inſtantly vowed not to ſtirre a foot farther, except with baggage, and that the women might be fetch'd over, which was done accordingly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94c51874-c3d8-4916-b6aa-9e01f5273ef9",
                                                "sense_id": "5e7f29d8-0251-3ca7-b6aa-4d45a614c7e4",
                                                "text": "No Dangers threatned, but they ſmil'd to meet\n The pannick French-men trembling at their Feet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "panic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f6c89fe-dd70-3284-bb17-c6679b129cab",
                                        "entry_id": "1725f6a4-ab77-37d6-81da-ebfd041e04b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Overwhelming fear or fright, often affecting groups of people or animals; (countable) an instance of this; a fright, a scare."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "301b543a-ecc8-4656-b06f-a44bbb79ba97",
                                                "sense_id": "0f6c89fe-dd70-3284-bb17-c6679b129cab",
                                                "text": "She wakened in sharp panic, bewildered by the grotesquerie of some half-remembered dream in contrast with the harshness of inclement fact, drowsily realizing that since she had fallen asleep it had come on to rain smartly out of a shrouded sky."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "748dec14-25ea-44fa-ac5b-8a4224853fe4",
                                                "sense_id": "0f6c89fe-dd70-3284-bb17-c6679b129cab",
                                                "text": "There is no confusion like the confusion of a simple mind, and as we drove away Tom was feeling the hot whips of panic. His wife and his mistress, until an hour ago secure and inviolate, were slipping precipitately from his control."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10f13acc-f441-4ea5-90c1-7ad42b15fcb5",
                                                "sense_id": "0f6c89fe-dd70-3284-bb17-c6679b129cab",
                                                "text": "Meanwhile Nanny Broome was recovering from her initial panic and seemed anxious to make up for any kudos she might have lost, by exerting her personality to the utmost. She took the policeman's helmet and placed it on a chair, and unfolded his tunic to shake it and fold it up again for him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af0066ef-36b7-4344-b9d4-762d6cd54f0a",
                                                "sense_id": "0f6c89fe-dd70-3284-bb17-c6679b129cab",
                                                "text": "It's Christmas at ground zero\n There's panic in the crowd\n We can dodge debris\n While we trim the tree\n Underneath a mushroom cloud"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5003ee2-0513-4baa-ba92-8653a957da6a",
                                                "sense_id": "0f6c89fe-dd70-3284-bb17-c6679b129cab",
                                                "text": "With a bolt of fright he remembered that there was no bathroom in the Hobhouse Room. He leapt along the corridor in a panic, stopping by the long-case clock at the end where he flattened himself against the wall."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c16d698b-4d18-3766-b329-a104d30c73bb",
                                        "entry_id": "1725f6a4-ab77-37d6-81da-ebfd041e04b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of kernel panic (“on Unix-derived operating systems: an action taken by the operating system when it cannot recover from a fatal error”); (by extension) any computer system crash."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46e5a129-6763-4033-94b7-0fc1b220e3a6",
                                                "sense_id": "c16d698b-4d18-3766-b329-a104d30c73bb",
                                                "text": "If your new driver has an error that panics the system when you load the driver, then the system will panic again when it tries to reboot after the panic. The system will continue the cycle of panic, reboot, and panic as it attempts to reload the faulty driver every time it reboots after panic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1859e867-3448-310c-913d-c208bc69499e",
                                        "entry_id": "1725f6a4-ab77-37d6-81da-ebfd041e04b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rapid reduction in asset prices due to broad efforts to raise cash in anticipation of such prices continuing to decline."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ebb9241-e512-4798-8f4b-6574fc1f4b72",
                                                "sense_id": "1859e867-3448-310c-913d-c208bc69499e",
                                                "text": "\"I thought you inherited your money.\"\n \"I did, old sport,\" he said automatically, \"but I lost most of it in the big panic—the panic of the war.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bff5f4da-ad96-42e8-8a9d-d08ef6b5d673",
                                                "sense_id": "1859e867-3448-310c-913d-c208bc69499e",
                                                "text": "\"There is sort of a panic going on, and that is not what ought to be,\" [Chris] Dodd, a Democrat from Connecticut, said at a press conference in Washington today. \"Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac were never bottom feeders in the residential mortgage market.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d10045b0-284e-32cb-a54a-bae8eb1bd7da",
                                        "entry_id": "1725f6a4-ab77-37d6-81da-ebfd041e04b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A highly amusing or entertaining performer, performance, or show; a riot, a scream."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "panic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41c4a859-fd9b-3946-8df6-bdb64ea015b4",
                                        "entry_id": "33c03675-b6b9-3791-88f4-3632f4f7bfea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause (someone) to feel panic (“overwhelming fear or fright”); also, to frighten (someone) into acting hastily."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92d4e1bb-729c-48e1-9be7-dae4d401e7db",
                                                "sense_id": "41c4a859-fd9b-3946-8df6-bdb64ea015b4",
                                                "text": "He told us he'd almost stepped on Ellen's body that night—dead and stiffening. Then I'd come round the corner and hailed him, and that panicked him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2eed9f5d-2913-330d-a60c-2b3418ede76f",
                                        "entry_id": "33c03675-b6b9-3791-88f4-3632f4f7bfea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause (a computer system) to crash."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "495d0066-5940-44d3-a4d6-d25b8c0ff910",
                                                "sense_id": "2eed9f5d-2913-330d-a60c-2b3418ede76f",
                                                "text": "If your new driver has an error that panics the system when you load the driver, then the system will panic again when it tries to reboot after the panic. The system will continue the cycle of panic, reboot, and panic as it attempts to reload the faulty driver every time it reboots after panic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "62b992aa-2fc1-3da1-a521-953ca405672f",
                                        "entry_id": "33c03675-b6b9-3791-88f4-3632f4f7bfea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To highly amuse, entertain, or impress (an audience watching a performance or show)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7589caf0-e605-3ef8-b1b9-cacb35836bce",
                                        "entry_id": "33c03675-b6b9-3791-88f4-3632f4f7bfea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To feel panic, or overwhelming fear or fright; to freak out, to lose one's head."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ea81936-7171-48cb-ac0c-36c18148d351",
                                                "sense_id": "7589caf0-e605-3ef8-b1b9-cacb35836bce",
                                                "text": "I don't want you to be hopeful, I want you to panic. I want you to feel the fear I feel every day and then I want you to act."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37c33c0d-6a9c-3535-8a04-a28d0231af8a",
                                        "entry_id": "33c03675-b6b9-3791-88f4-3632f4f7bfea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a computer system: to crash."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
